# sln-geo-aux-heat milling config, v2
#
# Verified against pcb2gcode 3.0.4 (same version you run). Two changes from v1,
# both necessary; neither works without the other.
#
# 1. FIXED COORDINATE FRAME.  v1 had zero-start=1, which derives the origin
#    from the job's bounding box.  Widening the isolation pushes the outermost
#    pass ~23 mil further out, which moves that bounding box, which silently
#    shifts EVERY output including the drill file.  Measured: the drill G-code
#    moved dX -0.0234, dY +0.0234 in between v1-narrow and v1-wide with
#    identical drill data.
#
#    zero-start=0 with explicit offsets pins the frame.  Verified: the drill
#    file is byte-identical (md5 5c412c1bfd0d) across single-pass, 0.030
#    isolation, and two-tool configs.
#
#    The offsets below are chosen so this fixed frame lands exactly where your
#    v1 output landed, which keeps the probe map, kicad_regions.py, the area-1
#    polygon and the Edge_Cuts profile all valid.  Note x-offset is -MX and
#    y-offset is MY from kicad_regions.py - same constants, as expected.
#
# 2. ISOLATION WIDTH.  v1 cut one pass at the tool width, leaving 7.3 mil from
#    each ESP32 pad to the surrounding copper plus a floating copper fragment
#    between adjacent pads.  isolation-width=0.030 clears the whole gap:
#    measured 19.7 mil pad-to-copper, zero floating fragments.  19.7 mil is
#    your 0.5 mm pour clearance - that is the ceiling, because past that the
#    pour is real copper pcb2gcode must keep.  So this reproduces the design.
#
#    Cost: isolation goes from 87.2 in / 9.7 min to 456.4 in / 50.7 min at F9.
#
#    A second larger mill bit does NOT help - tested.  mill-diameters with
#    0.0073,0.03125 still runs all 456.4 in on the V-bit and adds 59.1 in on
#    the second tool.  It does not replace V-bit passes.  Single tool is right.

software=linuxcnc

back=sln-geo-aux-heat-B_Cu.gbr
drill=sln-geo-aux-heat.drl

output-dir=out
basename=geoaux

mill-diameters=0.0073
isolation-width=0.030
milling-overlap=60%
zwork=-0.002
mill-feed=9
mill-vertfeed=5
mill-speed=10000

drills-available=0.032,0.0465,0.0625,0.125
zdrill=-0.075
drill-feed=25
drill-speed=10000
nog81=1

zsafe=0.1
zchange=1.0

# fixed frame - do NOT reintroduce zero-start
zero-start=0
x-offset=-4.3372
y-offset=3.2478
